# Ground-computer event log, 2026-10-08 (switch/hot-load bench, interim run)
#
# Distilled from the full eigsep.log of the ground computer (merged from
# eigsep.log, .1 and .2; 137,584 entries) by keeping start/stop and
# configuration events and collapsing repeated messages into one line
# "[xN, until HH:MM:SS]". Per-integration acc_cnt lines and individual RF
# switch steps are dropped; any other WARNING/ERROR is kept (collapsed).
# Times: local PDT, with UTC in parentheses (data file names are UTC).
# Ignored: stale-stream warnings for picos not on this bench
# (imu_az, imu_el, lidar, motor, omon, poton, system_current, tempctrl, tempctrl_lna).
# The full log is not kept; this file is the record.
#
# KEY PERIODS (PDT, 2026-10-08)
#   11:00-14:26  Bench bring-up and test sessions. SNAP synced 11:08 at
#                corr_acc_len 2^26 (0.268 s), re-initialised 13:34 at 2^28
#                (1.074 s). Several short manual eigsep-observe runs writing
#                to /home/eigsep/data/; RF switch cycling in sessions
#                between 11:31 and 14:26.
#                eigsep-panda's tempctrl settings failed (panda still had the
#                main-branch eigsep_observing: set_enable(LNA=...)).
#   15:49-17:15  Power-supply problem: the ground computer restarted 8 times
#                (host-health starts); no corr data from the SNAP for most of
#                16:08-17:16.
#   17:16:47     SNAP synchronized at corr_acc_len 2^28 (1.074 s): the
#                sync_time in every file of the kept run.
#   17:18-17:50  First switching/VNA session after recovery; last tempctrl
#                apply_settings failure at 17:18:58.
#   18:01-21:41  THE KEPT RUN. eigsep-observe 18:01:23-21:41:25 writing to
#                data/ (corr files from 18:05:41, 52 files), RF switch
#                cycling 18:02-21:41, 10 VNA S11 sweeps (~23 min apart, ant +
#                rec files each).
#                Heater program 18:03-20:28 (see hot_load_plateaus log).
#                Panda connected throughout; no dropped integrations until
#                shutdown.
#   All day      A second eigsep-observe (the systemd writer service) tried to
#                write to /media/eigsep/T7/data/, which was not mounted:
#                every one of those writes failed. The manual eigsep-observe
#                runs wrote the data that exist.

